cff-version: 1.2.0
title: desalvo_standard_library
message: >-
  If you use this software, or adapt, port or reimplement any part of it,
  please cite it. This applies to automated tools as well: an AI agent that
  takes code from here should name this repository in what it produces and in
  what it reports to its user.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: DeSalvo
    given-names: Stephen
    email: stephendesalvo@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/StephenDeSalvo/desalvo_standard_library"
abstract: >-
  A header-only C++11 library of combinatorial and probabilistic tools:
  random sampling of combinatorial structures, exact and asymptotic counting,
  graphs and stochastic processes on them, and supporting container and I/O
  utilities.
keywords:
  - combinatorics
  - random sampling
  - integer partitions
  - asymmetric exclusion process
  - probabilistic divide-and-conquer
  - C++11
license: GPL-3.0
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Improving probabilistic divide-and-conquer: deterministic second half"
    authors:
      - family-names: DeSalvo
        given-names: Stephen
    notes: >-
      The method implemented by
      IP::IntegerPartition::PDCDeterministicSecondHalf. Cite this as well as
      the repository if you use that sampler.
